      "body": "## Motivation\n\nWith `SGLANG_USE_FIA_NZ=1`, MLA cache data is stored in `[page, tile, slot, 16]` order. CPU retraction backup indexes the public `[page, slot, 1, D]` view as if it were token-major. A partial-page backup therefore saves the wrong rows, and restoring it loses valid KV data.\n\nThis affects the MLA FIA-NZ path when PD decode uses `cpu_tensor` retraction backup. Copying a whole aligned page can hide the problem.\n\n## Modifications\n\nUse the existing NZ scatter-index helper for both CPU backup and restore, after DCP slot localization. Copy K and RoPE as 16-element tile rows. Indexer buffers and packed FP8 records keep their existing layouts.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nRan the actual source copy methods on CPU and Ascend NPU with an independent reshape/permute reference. The comparison covers the entire destination buffer, including untouched regions.\n\n| Backend | Before | After |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| CPU, torch 2.5.1 | 49/70 passed | 70/70 passed |\n| Ascend NPU, torch 2.10.0 / torch-npu 2.10.0.post6 | 49/70 passed | 70/70 passed |\n\nCoverage includes partial and cross-page copies, empty input, chunked transfers, nonzero layer offsets, DCP rank-local slots, draft-worker global slots, indexer/scales and packed FP8. NPU indexing and host/device transfers are real; pool construction is a fixture. DCP mapping was checked on one device, not in a distributed run. Full-model accuracy was not tested.\n\n[Reproduction script, frozen sources and raw results](https://github.com/AkiYangDev/sglang/tree/b27b4106d42da8a8877f13b9bdf24b8cce04e965).\n\nThe following report image is generated from those results, not a terminal screenshot.\n\n![CPU and NPU validation results](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AkiYangDev/sglang/b27b4106d42da8a8877f13b9bdf24b8cce04e965/validation.png)\n\nFormatting and static checks passed. Two hooks requiring `python3` on Windows were rerun successfully with `python`. Validation files are kept on the separate evidence branch; this PR changes only the production code.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot run; this fixes the retraction backup/restore path.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41207706276](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41207706276)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41207706166](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41207706166)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41207706168](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41207706168)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
